// The G1 GATE merge-class example (`.design/stage1-forge-tier.md` REQ-10 / AC-14, the
// stage-1 gate's centerpiece). A SINGLE `fn` whose certificate exhibits the forge tier
// end to end: out-of-cage clauses no longer degrade DOWN the ladder — each ESCALATES
// to the engine that grounds it, and the item certifies at the MIN over its clauses.
//
// `merge_class` is a merge/binary-search MIDPOINT selector: `result = (lo + hi) / 2`,
// the index a merge step splits its run at. Its contract carries three clauses at the
// three forge rungs, all GROUNDED in `forge/src/relax.rs::classify_fn` (the relaxable
// fragment gate):
//
//   * `ens#0  lo + 1 <= hi + 1`          — a RELAXABLE universally-quantified polynomial
//   * `ens#1  2 * lo <= lo + hi`            atom (no div/mod/shift/cast): the merge index
//                                           side-conditions. Each routes to the
//                                           [`NlsatEngine`] real relaxation (QF_NRA) and,
//                                           real-valid by the kernel-checked `r_relax_sound`,
//                                           certifies at **L4** (kernel-grounded).
//
//   * `ens#2  result * 2 + (lo + hi) % 2 == lo + hi`
//                                         — NOT relaxable (the `%` is not a polynomial
//                                           atom — `classify_fn` rejects it), so it routes
//                                           to the Lean engine. It is the div/mod identity
//                                           pinning `result` to the midpoint; discharged at
//                                           **L3** by an author-authored, frozen-battery
//                                           proof (`simp` over the frozen denotation simp-set
//                                           + `omega`), kernel-accepted and axiom-gated. The
//                                           certificate carries the BURN RECEIPT (the proof's
//                                           lexer-token count + cited frozen simp-lemmas).
//
// The item level is the MIN over the clauses — **L3** (clauses L4, L4, L3). The
// `witness` block makes `merge_class` covenant-routed: the author `inhabit` witnesses are
// executed against `req` and the fixed-seed `falsify` run rides the body → `ens`, so the
// certificate carries the COVENANT EVIDENCE block (covenant-before-burn, R-COV-1). The
// forge/Lean discharge also pins the definition-tower MEANING AUDIT (anti-Goodhart) and
// the re-elaboration MUTATION score. All four forge-tier evidence blocks populated — the
// AC-14 checklist, in one certificate.
fn merge_class(lo: u64, hi: u64) -> u64
    req lo <= hi
    ens lo + 1 <= hi + 1
    ens 2 * lo <= lo + hi
    ens result * 2 + (lo + hi) % 2 == lo + hi
    fx pure
{ (lo + hi) / 2 }

witness { inhabit (0, 0); inhabit (2, 7); falsify 64; }

proof for merge_class {
    ens#2 by { simp [Thermite.denote, Thermite.Env.bindInt, Thermite.intVal, Thermite.arithDenote]; omega }
}
